From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:45:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: custody-v2-e2e on the original book-bound vault
 (2-argument constructor)

custody-v2-e2e deployed the pinned variant's 3-argument constructor against
contracts/EnclaveSecretVaultV2.sol, the restored production source whose
constructor is (book, enclaveOwner), and failed before any member code ran.

It now uses the reviewed original-vault rig (test/helpers/original-vault-rig.mjs
and the deployed schema-4 registry source test/fixtures/EnclaveRegistry.schema4.sol,
both byte-identical to the reviewed custody-v2-original-vault-e2e tree), the
book-kind reader, and the address-book authority semantics of that vault: the
admin's book names the ledger and registry; a cleared registry fails release
closed and a restore recovers. The pinned variant's "book edits cannot disable
release" assertion does not hold for this vault and is replaced.

Each machine persists through the daemon's real sealed-state writer (member
store + chain checkpoint). A failed genesis share write reaches no chain; every
createCommittee/ackHandover is checked against what its machine had durably; one
ack submission fails after the share is durable, that machine restarts from its
disk and re-acks the same share, which the contract accepts and activates.
No contract source changes.
